## 7. Rate-Limit Implementation Design

### 7.1 Store Interface (`apps/api/src/auth/rateLimitStore.ts`)
```typescript
export interface RateLimitStore {
  increment(key: string, windowMs: number, limit: number): Promise<RateLimitResult>;
  get(key: string): Promise<RateLimitResult | null>;
  reset(key: string): Promise<void>;
  cleanup(): Promise<void>;  // remove expired entries
}

export interface RateLimitResult {
  allowed: boolean;
  current: number;
  limit: number;
  remaining: number;
  resetAt: number;  // Unix ms
  retryAfterMs?: number;
}
```

### 7.2 PostgreSQL Implementation (`apps/api/src/auth/postgresRateLimitStore.ts`)
```sql
-- Migration: rate_limit_counters table
CREATE TABLE rate_limit_counters (
  key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  window_start TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  window_ms BIGINT NOT NULL,
  limit INTEGER NOT NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
CREATE INDEX idx_rate_limit_window ON rate_limit_counters (window_start);
```

Atomic increment via:
```sql
INSERT INTO rate_limit_counters (key, count, window_start, window_ms, limit)
VALUES ($1, 1, now(), $2, $3)
ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET
  count = rate_limit_counters.count + 1,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE rate_limit_counters.window_start > now() - rate_limit_counters.window_ms * interval '1 ms'
RETURNING count, window_start;
```

### 7.3 Rate Limiter (`apps/api/src/auth/rateLimiter.ts`)
```typescript
export class RateLimiter {
  constructor(
    private store: RateLimitStore,
    private policies: RateLimitPolicy[],
    private failClosed: boolean = true  // for AI generation
  ) {}
  
  async check(request: RateLimitRequest): Promise<RateLimitResult> {
    // Match policy by route pattern + user/IP
    // Increment counter
    // Return 429 with Retry-After if exceeded
  }
}

export interface RateLimitPolicy {
  pattern: RegExp | string;  // route pattern
  scope: 'user' | 'ip' | 'user+ip';
  windowMs: number;
  limit: number;
  failClosed?: boolean;  // override for AI endpoints
}
```

### 7.4 Initial Policies (Configurable via Env)
| Endpoint Pattern | Scope | Window | Limit | Fail Closed |
|-----------------|-------|--------|-------|-------------|
| `/v0/conversations*` (POST messages) | user | 1 min | 10 | ✅ |
| `/v0/conversations*` (POST messages) | user | 1 hour | 60 | ✅ |
| `/v0/conversations` (POST create) | user | 1 min | 10 | ❌ |
| `/v0/*` (all) | ip | 1 min | 120 | ❌ |
| AI token budget | user | 24 hour | 100k tokens | ✅ |

### 7.5 Duplicate Submission Protection
- Client generates idempotency key per message (`clientRequestId`)
- Rate limiter checks `idempotency:{key}` before incrementing AI counters
- If key exists → return cached response, no AI generation charged

### 7.6 Fail-Safe Behavior
| Scenario | Behavior |
|----------|----------|
| DB unavailable | If `failClosed=true` → deny request (503); else allow (fail-open) |
| Counter cleanup | Background job runs hourly; removes entries older than 2x max window |
| Clock skew | Use DB `now()` for window boundaries |

