## 8. Security Considerations

### 8.1 Authentication
- [ ] All coaching routes require valid Supabase JWT
- [ ] `userId` derived from `JWT.sub` — never from URL params
- [ ] JWT verified via Supabase JWKS (rotating keys)
- [ ] Token expiry enforced (reject expired tokens)
- [ ] Refresh handled client-side by Supabase SDK

### 8.2 Authorization
- [ ] Conversation ownership: `conversation.user_id = auth.uid()`
- [ ] Message ownership: via conversation ownership
- [ ] Action execution: `action.user_id = auth.uid()` (enforced in registry)
- [ ] RLS policies on `conversations`, `conversation_messages`

### 8.3 API Key Protection
- [ ] `AI_API_KEY` only in server environment variables
- [ ] Never logged, never sent to frontend
- [ ] Rotated via Supabase/environment secret management
- [ ] Different keys per environment (dev/staging/prod)

### 8.4 Rate Limiting
- [ ] User-based limits prevent abuse
- [ ] IP-based limits prevent anonymous enumeration
- [ ] AI token budgets prevent cost overruns
- [ ] Fail-closed on AI endpoints when limiter unavailable

### 8.5 Data Protection
- [ ] Conversation content encrypted at rest (Supabase default)
- [ ] PII in conversations: user messages may contain health data — consider field-level encryption
- [ ] Audit trail immutable; no deletion of coaching turns

