## 11. Acceptance Criteria

### 11.1 Phase 9.5A — Foundation
- [ ] `npm run db:migrate` applies cleanly to Supabase PostgreSQL
- [ ] All coaching routes return 401 without valid Supabase JWT
- [ ] Valid JWT allows access; `userId` = `JWT.sub` (verified in tests)
- [ ] Cross-user access returns 403 (ownership enforced)
- [ ] Rate limiter returns 429 with `Retry-After` header when limits exceeded
- [ ] AI message limits: 10/min, 60/hour per user (configurable)
- [ ] General API limit: 120/min per IP
- [ ] Frontend sign-up → onboarding → coach flow works end-to-end
- [ ] No client-supplied `userId` in any coaching request
- [ ] RLS policies active on `conversations`, `conversation_messages`
- [ ] All existing Phase 9.4 tests pass with auth + rate limiter

### 11.2 Phase 9.5B — AI Provider
- [ ] `AI_PROVIDER=anthropic` starts AnthropicProvider; `mock` starts MockAIProvider
- [ ] Startup fails with clear error if `AI_PROVIDER=anthropic` but `AI_API_KEY` missing
- [ ] Structured output: `answer`, `proposedActions[]`, `reasoningTrace[]`, `confidence`, `tokenUsage`
- [ ] Function calling maps to action registry allowlist (7 actions)
- [ ] ResponseValidator still runs and catches hallucinations/contradictions
- [ ] Token usage tracked per request; persisted in response + audit log
- [ ] Daily token budget enforced via rate limiter (100k tokens/user/day default)
- [ ] Timeouts: 30s connect, 120s response; retries: 3x exponential backoff
- [ ] Fail-closed: provider error → 502/503, never silent mock fallback
- [ ] All 12 integration scenarios pass with real provider (mocked HTTP in CI)

### 11.3 Phase 9.5C — Hardening
- [ ] Duplicate message submission (same idempotency key) returns cached response
- [ ] Audit trail: every coaching turn logged with userId, conversationId, evidenceRefs, actions, execution results
- [ ] Structured JSON logs with correlation IDs; request/response sanitized
- [ ] `/health` endpoint returns `{ status, database, aiProvider, version }`
- [ ] Prometheus metrics: `coaching_turns_total`, `coaching_latency_seconds`, `provider_tokens_total`, `rate_limit_exceeded_total`
- [ ] Load test: 100 concurrent users, p95 < 2s per turn, 0% error rate
- [ ] No secrets in logs, code, tests, or Git history

