## 12. Test Requirements

### 12.1 Unit Tests
| Component | Tests |
|-----------|-------|
| `AnthropicProvider` | Structured output parsing, tool call mapping, token counting, retry logic, timeout handling, missing API key error |
| `ProviderFactory` | Config validation, provider selection, startup failure modes |
| `PostgresRateLimitStore` | Atomic increment, window expiry, cleanup, concurrent increments |
| `RateLimiter` | Policy matching, scope resolution, fail-closed/open, idempotency |
| `SupabaseAuth` | JWT verification, JWKS caching, expired token rejection |

### 12.2 Integration Tests
| Scenario | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Auth + coaching flow | Sign up → create conversation → send message → receive AI response |
| Rate limit enforcement | Exceed 10/min → 429 with Retry-After; wait → succeeds |
| Cross-user isolation | User A cannot access User B's conversations |
| AI token budget | Exceed daily token limit → 429 on AI endpoints only |
| Idempotency | Duplicate message with same key → cached response, no double charge |
| Provider failure | Anthropic 500 → 502 to client; no mock fallback |
| RLS enforcement | Direct DB query without auth returns 0 rows |

### 12.3 End-to-End Tests (Playwright)
| Flow | Steps |
|------|-------|
| New user onboarding | Visit app → sign up → complete onboarding → land on Home |
| Coach conversation | Navigate to Coach → new conversation → ask question → see evidence → propose action → confirm → see result |
| Rate limit UI | Send 11 messages rapidly → see 429 toast with retry countdown |
| Session persistence | Refresh page → conversation list preserved → continue conversation |

