## 13. Rollback Strategy

### 13.1 Database
| Risk | Rollback |
|------|----------|
| Migration fails | `prisma migrate resolve --rolled-back <migration_name>` |
| RLS breaks queries | `ALTER TABLE conversations DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` |
| Supabase auth sync broken | Drop trigger/function; revert to `userId` from URL (temp) |

### 13.2 AI Provider
| Risk | Rollback |
|------|----------|
| AnthropicProvider bugs | Set `AI_PROVIDER=mock` in env; immediate fallback |
| Token counting wrong | Disable token budget in rate limiter (`AI_TOKEN_BUDGET_ENABLED=false`) |
| Structured output parsing fails | Extend validator to handle malformed responses gracefully |

### 13.3 Rate Limiter
| Risk | Rollback |
|------|----------|
| DB unavailable → fail-closed blocks all | Set `RATE_LIMIT_FAIL_CLOSED=false` (fail-open) |
| Counter cleanup removes active | Increase cleanup interval; manual `DELETE` if needed |
| Wrong limits | Update env vars; no code deploy needed |

### 13.4 Frontend Auth
| Risk | Rollback |
|------|----------|
| Supabase SDK breaks | Revert to `SessionContext` with localStorage `userId` (Phase 9.4 behavior) |

---

## 14. Decisions Requiring Confirmation

| # | Decision | Options | Recommendation |
|---|----------|---------|----------------|
| 1 | **Supabase Auth Sync** | A) Application-level sync on sign-up<br>B) Database trigger on `auth.users` insert | **A** — simpler, explicit, testable |
| 2 | **RLS Scope** | A) Enable on `conversations`, `messages` only<br>B) Enable on all user-data tables | **A** — start minimal; expand after verification |
| 3 | **Connection Pooling** | A) PgBouncer (port 6543) for all runtime<br>B) Direct (5432) for migrations, pooled for runtime | **B** — standard Supabase pattern |
| 4 | **AI Provider Default** | A) Default to mock (`AI_PROVIDER=mock`)<br>B) Require explicit env var (fail startup if unset) | **B** — explicit configuration |
| 5 | **Token Counting** | A) Anthropic's token counting API (extra request)<br>B) Local approximation (tiktoken)<br>C) Skip for now, estimate from response | **B** — local, fast, accurate enough for budgets |
| 6 | **Idempotency Key Storage** | A) In `conversation_messages` table<br>B) Separate `idempotency_keys` table with TTL | **B** — cleaner separation, automatic expiry |
| 7 | **Audit Trail Retention** | A) 90 days<br>B) 1 year<br>C) Indefinite (archive to cold storage) | **A** — start with 90 days, configurable |
| 8 | **Rate Limit Config Format** | A) JSON in env var<br>B) TypeScript config file (compiled)<br>C) Database table (admin UI later) | **A** — simple, deploy-time configurable |
| 9 | **Frontend Session Storage** | A) Supabase SDK handles (localStorage + memory)<br>B) Custom secure storage | **A** — use SDK defaults |
| 10 | **Provider Fallback Order** | A) Anthropic → OpenAI → Mock<br>B) Anthropic → Mock only<br>C) Configurable chain | **B** — simpler; OpenAI added later if needed |

